// boxcxx — <__bits/version_bitset>
//
// The [support.limits.general] per-header slot for <bitset>. It carries
// P2697R1's __cpp_lib_bitset -- the string_view constructor -- and not
// __cpp_lib_constexpr_bitset, the one C++23 macro this header owns, which
// is not claimable yet (see <version>'s omission list -- the string-taking
// constructor and both to_string() forms cannot run in constant evaluation
// because basic_string is not constexpr). Everything else in [template.
// bitset] IS constexpr, so the moment the constexpr_string blocker lifts
// the define goes back here and nothing else has to move.
//
// Same split rationale as <__bits/version_any>/<__bits/version_complex> --
// see those files' comments.
//
// Every block below is gated on BOXCXX_OWNS_<stem>, and this file has NO
// include guard: it is meant to be included once per owning header, each time
// defining only what that header declared it owns. [support.limits.general]
// says a macro is defined by <version> AND by the header that provides the
// feature; it does not say every header that happens to include this leaf.
// A header that answers for a feature it does not provide is answering a
// question it was not asked, so it no longer does. <version> defines
// BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL and takes the lot. Checked by tools/cxx_ftm_audit.sh.

// P2697R1 -- explicit bitset(basic_string_view<CharT, Traits>, pos, n,
// zero, one). Independent of the constexpr_bitset blocker above: the new
// constructor is as constexpr as the rest of the class, it is the string
// one that is not.
#if (defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL) || defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_bitset)) && \
    !defined(__cpp_lib_bitset)
#  define __cpp_lib_bitset 202306L
#endif
#undef BOXCXX_OWNS_bitset
